  artifactSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 9e6ef4024b65a5f4eb9b3926d2917e2e, type: 3}
  plaqueTitle: General Malvar Field Saddle
  plaqueDescription: This saddle represents the perseverance of Filipino military
    leaders who continued resisting American forces during the later years of the
    Philippine-American War.
  artifactInspectionDescription: Crafted from thick, conditioned cowhide over a wooden
    saddle tree. Heavy brass rivets and cinch buckles secure the stirrup leathers,
    showing genuine battle-worn patina from campaigns across Luzon.
  initialDialogue: what should i do
